# Godot
.godot/
.import/

# Third-party addons, reinstalled per machine — see docs/tooling.md. Ignored by
# default because they are large (at-icons alone is 21 MB) and re-downloadable.
# project.godot keeps the [editor_plugins] enable line — Godot warns and skips
# if the addon is absent, which is non-fatal.
addons/*

# The exception, and why it has to exist: an *asset* a scene preloads is not
# tooling. A missing addon plugin is a warning; a missing icon a panel preloads
# is a hard load failure on a fresh clone, and tools/run_tests.sh runs headless
# straight from the repo. So every at-icons file src/ actually references is
# committed at its res:// path with `git add -f`, and the licence travels with
# it. Nothing under src/ may reference an addon file that is not committed.
!addons/at-icons/
addons/at-icons/*
!addons/at-icons/LICENSE.txt

# The second exception, V2.4b, and it is a different KIND: dialogue_manager is
# not an asset reference but the project's FIRST GAME RUNTIME dependency. The
# summit scenes run through it in shipped builds, so a fresh clone without it is
# a broken game, not a warning -- which is exactly the at-icons argument with
# `src/` replaced by `the game itself`. Committed whole (790 KB, 122 files,
# MIT, upstream re-downloadable), autoload registered in the COMMITTED
# project.godot, and the no-autoloads exception is stated where CLAUDE.md
# prices it rather than arrived at because the editor put it there.
!addons/dialogue_manager/

# Sample content AssetLib downloads unpack into the project root rather than
# under addons/. Same reasoning as the rule above — large, re-downloadable, and
# not this game: road_demos/ is road generation, demo/ is a combat sample with
# agents and fireballs. Kept on disk so the demos still open in the editor.
road_demos/
demo/
@icons picker.html

# The Godot MCP bridge registration. Per-machine by construction -- it names an
# absolute path to a globally-installed npm package, and the addon it talks to is
# itself gitignored above. Regenerate it from Project -> Tools -> MCP Toolkit ->
# Write .mcp.json, or copy the form in docs/tooling.md. tools/check_mcp.sh says
# so out loud when it is missing.
.mcp.json

export.cfg
export_presets.cfg
*.translation

# Raw datasets — re-downloadable, never committed. See docs/data-sources.md
sources/

# Python bytecode from tools/import_data.py
__pycache__/

# Builds
build/
dist/
*.exe
*.pck
*.zip

# OS
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Obsidian editor UI state -- churns every session, no design content
.obsidian/workspace.json

# The vault exception, stated (the ultra pass-7 finding): the repo ROOT is the
# documentation vault -- AGENTS.md's own opening instruction; the [[ROADMAP]]
# links do not resolve from anywhere else -- so .obsidian/ is COMMITTED, plugin
# bundles whole, so a fresh clone's documentation vault opens working. It is
# the dialogue_manager exception's documentation twin: a surface, not game
# code -- src/ reads nothing in it, which is also why tools/check_names.sh
# skips the tree. Plugin updates show as standing dirt, committed deliberately
# like project.godot's.
# EXCEPT the Local REST API plugin's data.json: it carries the Local REST API
# key -- per-machine, minted on first Obsidian load; the docker mcp secret
# store holds the working copy's value. A fresh clone regenerates it with its
# own key on first load, which is the correct per-machine behaviour. The local
# file stays on disk; the plugin needs it and the vault connection keeps
# working.
.obsidian/plugins/obsidian-local-rest-api/data.json

# Per-machine agent state, like .mcp.json above -- plans and scratch belonging to
# whichever assistant is driving, not to this game.
.zcode/
# .codex/config.toml registers the Godot MCP bridge by an absolute path on this
# machine -- the same per-machine fact as .mcp.json, tracked by mistake until 2026-10-14.
.codex/
.zcodeignore
.mimosa/
docs/superpowers/
# .v2c/plugin_root holds one absolute path into .zcode/ above, so it is the
# same per-machine fact one directory over.
.v2c/

# Agent vision scratch (godot-agent-vision skill) — captures never stage
.gdskills/

# Session dev reports (playtests, probes, reviews) — local working record, never staged
reports/
tools/_fetch_born.py
tools/portraits_counterparts.json
tools/_apply_corrections.py
tools/_merge_traits.py
tools/fetch_photos.py
tools/portraits_photo_sources.json

# The review fleet's working dir (file snapshots, diffs, comment fetches the
# ultra's lenses leave mid-pass). Gitignored so a running pass never drowns
# git status -- and EMPTIED at every block closeout, same rule as the
# .superpowers/sdd scratch: working space, not storage. The * catches the
# per-PR suffix a pass appends (.review-tmp48/ and friends).
.review-tmp*
.review_tmp*
.review-tmp*.gd
.review_tmp*.gd
# The audit fleet's root-level fetch scratch (PR comment dumps), plus the
# Windows `nul` redirect artifact its subshells keep minting.
pr4*.md
pr4*.json
pr4*.txt
nul
